course: dictionary
lesson: 15366
title: Sourness: taste and mood
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sourness is a noun, a name for a thing. It has two main meanings. The first is a sharp, acid taste, like lemons or vinegar. The second is a bad-tempered, bitter or unfriendly mood or feeling.
explain: Look at the words around it to choose the meaning. «The sourness of the lemon made Sam pull a face.» The lemon is something you taste, so sourness means the sharp taste. «The sourness in Mia's voice showed she was still cross about losing.» Here it means an unfriendly, bitter mood.
explain: Test your choice by putting the meaning into the sentence. Try "the sharp taste of the lemon" or "the bitter mood in her voice". If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Sourness is an uncountable noun, so we do not say "a sourness" or "two sournesses".
fact: Sourness is one of the five basic tastes, along with sweet, salty, bitter and umami.
fact: Sourness comes from acids, such as the acid in lemons and vinegar.
fact: «Sourness» can also describe a feeling, as in «the sourness between the two friends after the argument».
fact: The adjective «sour» goes with the same ideas: «a sour lemon» or «a sour face».
exercise: «The sourness of the lemon made Sam pull a face.» What does sourness mean here? | A loud, noisy crowd | *A sharp, acid taste | A happy, sweet smell | A tired, sleepy feeling
exercise: «The sourness in Mia's voice showed she was still cross about losing.» What does sourness mean here? | A soft, gentle sound | *A bitter, unfriendly mood | A cheerful, friendly mood | A cold, icy wind
exercise: Which basic taste comes from acids, like the acid in lemons? | *Sourness | Softness | Sweetness | Saltiness
test: «The vinegar had a strong sourness that made Ben cough.» Which meaning fits? | A big, heavy box | A cheerful, happy mood | A soft, gentle sound | *A sharp, acid taste
test: «After the argument, the sourness between the two friends lasted for weeks.» What does sourness show here? | Hunger | *Bitterness and unfriendliness | Happiness | Coldness from the weather
exam: Which sentence uses sourness correctly? | «The sourness sang loudly in the rain.» | «The sourness ran quickly down the hill.» | *«The sourness of the lemon juice made Tom's mouth pucker.» | «He sourness three apples at lunch.»
